    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21429" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Īgŭvĭum</span></b> ,
			ĭi, n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a city of Umbria</i>, now <i>Gubbio</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att. 7, 13</span></i>, b, 6; <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				1, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 45, 43</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			461</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Īgŭ-vĭnātes</span></b> ,
				ium, m., <i>its
				inhabitants</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Balb. 20, 47</span></i>; and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Īgŭvīni</span></b> ,
				ōrum, m., <i><span class="en">Caes. B. C.
				1, 12</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 15, 7, 7, § 31</span></i>; and
				<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Iguini</span></b> , <i><span class="en">id. 3, 14,
				19, § 113</span></i>.</div>
